  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thanks for checking with us before acting. The payroll verification email you heard about is not legitimate. It was caught by our email filter and is held in quarantine, so it should not be in your inbox. Please do not click any link in it, reply to it, or enter your password anywhere. Our IT team never asks you to verify your payroll login by email. If you already clicked a link or entered your password, please tell us right away so we can secure your account. Your payroll is not affected by this message. A technician will review the sender and block it if needed. If you have questions about payroll, please contact HR or payroll directly through a known contact.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket from aisha.khan (user_id 5, HR Generalist, active, not blocked, no failed logins, password last set 2026-09-11). Quarantine check shows Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (capital I in place of l, lookalike domain), subject 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-10 21:36 UTC, reason phishing, NOT releasable. Not released; release is refused for phishing per KB-008. Other quarantined items (Q-1001, Q-1002) are generic spam and unrelated. The user reports only hearing about the email, not interacting with it, but she was a recipient, so per KB-008 this is escalated for security review: sender domain blocking and whether other users received it. Not yet confirmed whether user clicked or entered credentials. If she did, KB-029 applies (P1: sign-in log review, block_sign_in, reset_password). Recommend Tier 2 confirm with the user and check sign-in logs for user_id 5 around 2026-10-10 21:36 UTC onward. Also check other mailboxes for the same sender and subject.",
